  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dzud Disaster Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the United Nation&apos;s Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs, almost 60% of the total territory of Mongolia is experiencing a disaster called dzud, since the second half of December 2023, putting vulnerable herder households at serious risk and requiring a humanitarian response.Considering the scope of damages caused by the dzud and the government&apos;s constrained resources, it is recommended that an amount of $2.8 million is provided to the government as a grant financed by the APDRF, and up to 30% of the grant amount may be used retroactively for eligible expenditures incurred prior to grant effectiveness but not earlier than 8 December 2023 i.e. on the day the government activated its response through emergency operation centers.</narrative>
  </description>
